"""Context-specific interpretation for the original twelve references."""
DETAILS={
'fortigate-cli-essentials':['Record the model, firmware and current VDOM so later output is interpreted in the right context.','Compare CPU and memory with the incident window and a known baseline; capture at least two samples.','Find the affected interfaces, addresses and administrative state. Compare the WAN and LAN sides with the intended topology.','Identify the best matching destination prefix, next hop and outgoing interface. Check the return path on the peer separately.'],
'cisco-ios-essentials':['Record the device model and IOS or IOS XE release before comparing commands with documentation.','Find the management interface and compare its IP address, Status and Protocol with the expected state.','Inspect the affected port’s detailed line protocol, errors and recent counters. A cumulative counter needs a timed comparison.','Review only the relevant management interface and addressing configuration. Protect the output because it can contain sensitive settings.'],
'fortigate-routing-arp':['Replace <destination-ip> with the affected destination. Note the chosen prefix, gateway and interface.','Compare other active routes for the same destination or a more-specific prefix.','Find the next-hop address in the ARP table when it is directly connected; absence can mean it has not recently been contacted.','Inspect ARP details and the relevant interface; an unresolved neighbor suggests a local link or peer issue, not necessarily a remote routing problem.'],
'cisco-interface-diagnostics':['Identify the affected interface and compare IP address, administrative state and protocol.','Check switch-port state and negotiated link attributes on the relevant port.','Capture error counters twice with timestamps; rising CRC or input errors are stronger evidence than one old nonzero value.','Use descriptions to identify the intended connection, then verify the peer and cabling because labels can be stale.'],
'fortigate-vpn-health':['Locate the tunnel by peer or name and record its status and counters.','Inspect phase 2 selectors and security associations for the actual source and destination subnets.','Confirm the expected IKE gateway and remote peer; a missing gateway or unexpected peer narrows the problem.','Find the route to the remote service and confirm the egress interface points toward the expected VPN; also check the return path.'],
'cisco-vlans-trunks':['Find the endpoint access port and its assigned VLAN. A defined VLAN alone does not prove that it reaches the gateway.','On both ends of the uplink compare trunk state and the allowed and active VLAN lists.','Inspect the access port and uplink switchport mode, including native VLAN where relevant.','Look for the endpoint MAC in the correct VLAN and note the learned port; an inactive endpoint can age out.'],
'fortigate-ha-system-health':['Record the cluster members, roles and synchronization status without initiating a failover.','Check time synchronization on the member under investigation; compare time sources and timestamps.','Record firmware and appliance identity so both members can be compared.','Read diagnostic HA details and compare member health with the expected cluster state.'],
'cisco-routing-basics':['Locate the destination prefix and note the selected route source, next hop and outgoing interface.','Substitute the specific destination address and confirm the most-specific matching route.','If the next hop is directly connected, compare its IP and MAC mapping with the local segment.','Confirm the outgoing interface has the expected address and operational state. An up interface does not prove end-to-end reachability.'],
'fortigate-session-inspection':['Check current session totals and record the sample time. Compare a second sample during the incident with the normal session count for this appliance; a high count alone does not identify which traffic is responsible.','Compare session statistics with an established baseline for this appliance.','Inspect the relevant source, destination, translated addresses, policy and interfaces. Filter appropriately for your release before listing a large table.','Compare the active route for the same destination; record the time because an existing session may reflect an earlier forwarding decision.'],
'cisco-neighbor-discovery':['Identify the local uplink and advertised Cisco neighbor on that port.','Inspect neighbor details, including remote port and device identity, and compare with the topology record.','Check LLDP where enabled on both sides; a missing LLDP entry can reflect configuration or peer support.','Compare the manually maintained interface description with the discovered neighbor and physical cabling record.'],
'linux-network-essentials':['Identify the interface carrying the affected traffic and compare its address and prefix with the intended subnet.','Find the default or more-specific route and note its gateway and source interface.','Inspect the neighbor state for a directly connected gateway; incomplete or failed resolution suggests a local path issue.','Compare link errors and drops across two timed samples to see whether counters are increasing.'],
'cloud-network-fundamentals':['Compare source and destination prefixes to establish whether traffic is local or requires a routed path.','Identify the source and destination subnets, address ranges and the service endpoint.','Trace each applicable route table and next hop, including the return direction.','Compare the relevant stateful security rules with the required source, destination, protocol and port.','Resolve the service name from the workload’s environment and compare the result with the intended private address.']}
